// PIN ZYJS-010 — a module's function ran in the CALLER's scope.
//
// Two halves of one defect, both found by validating against the LDV
// applications and both closed 2026-08-30:
//
//   · a sibling's write was invisible.  `leer()` calls `_asegurar()`, which
//     builds the module's state, and then read the `#0` the module starts
//     with — because the frame carried a COPY of that state instead of the
//     module's own scope.  ZyBank's locale dispatcher is exactly this shape
//     and died four locales down with `$? not supported on bool`.
//
//   · a bare-name call found the caller's variable.  `saluda()` calls its own
//     `idiomas()`, and this file deliberately names a local array the same
//     thing.  `klingon_galaxy` does exactly that — an array of locales named
//     after the function that produces it — and the call died with
//     `'…' is not a function`.
//
// The rule both Rust engines follow: a function's frame sits over the globals
// of the file it was WRITTEN in.  For a function from another file that scope
// is live and shared, because module state is mutable; for one written here it
// is copied, so a write inside dies with the call (ERROR-ZYB-002).
<# ./module_state/lib => L

// El nombre choca a propósito con la función del módulo.
idiomas = ["a", "b"]

>> L::leer() ¶
>> L::saluda() ¶
>> (idiomas$#) ¶
